# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "One group index per term is enforced {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"
msgstr "Viene imposto un indice di gruppo per termine {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The groups array holds one index per term, and assigning one of a different length raises. Nothing downstream re-checks the invariant, so it is enforced where the indices enter the operator: an array that is too short would silently drop trailing terms, and one that is too long would invent groups that no term carries.\n"
msgstr "L'array dei gruppi contiene un indice per termine, e assegnarne uno di lunghezza diversa solleva un errore. Nessuna elaborazione a valle ricontrolla questo invariante, quindi viene imposto nel punto in cui gli indici entrano nell'operatore: un array troppo corto scarterebbe silenziosamente i termini finali, e uno troppo lungo inventerebbe gruppi che nessun termine possiede.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clearing the group indices by assigning `None` is always allowed.\n"
msgstr "Cancellare gli indici di gruppo assegnando `None` è sempre consentito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two checks are independent {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"
msgstr "I due controlli sono indipendenti {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") reports whether a group’s coefficients agree, which is the assumption [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") makes when it averages magnitudes. It is not a weaker form of the Hermiticity check: neither check implies the other, in either direction.\n"
msgstr "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") segnala se i coefficienti di un gruppo coincidono, che è l'assunzione fatta da [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") quando calcola la media delle magnitudini. Non è una forma più debole del controllo di hermiticità: nessuno dei due controlli implica l'altro, in nessuna direzione.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default the magnitudes are compared, because that is what [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") averages. A Hermitian conjugate pair with complex coefficients has equal magnitudes but unequal coefficients, so it satisfies only the default form.\n"
msgstr "Per impostazione predefinita vengono confrontate le magnitudini, perché è ciò di cui [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") calcola la media. Una coppia coniugata hermitiana con coefficienti complessi ha magnitudini uguali ma coefficienti diversi, quindi soddisfa solo la forma predefinita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") inherits the one-sided guarantee of [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): a `True` entry is always reliable, while a `False` entry is reliable only for operator types whose normal form is a genuine canonical form. Consult the specific operator type to find out which applies.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") eredita la garanzia unilaterale di [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): una voce `True` è sempre affidabile, mentre una voce `False` è affidabile solo per i tipi di operatore la cui forma normale è una vera forma canonica. Consulta il tipo di operatore specifico per sapere quale caso si applica.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

